  "originalQuery": "You work for a large financial services company that is expanding its operations globally. Your company plans to migrate to Google Cloud. You want a platform that scales easily, ensures low-latency transactions, and provides a reliable user experience for your customers. You need a storage layer for account information and financial transactions and want to maintain the existing relational schema used by your current platform. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Deploy Cloud Spanner using a multi-region instance, and place your compute resources close to the default leader region.<br/>B. Deploy Cloud Bigtable using a multi-region instance, and place your compute resources close to the default leader region.<br/>C. Build an in-memory cache in Memorystore, and deploy it to the specific geographic regions where your application resides.<br/>D. Use Cloud SQL with a high availability configuration, and deploy your compute resources in the same region as the primary instance.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
